{
  "unit": {
    "id": "3",
    "title": "What I did yesterday",
    "blurb": "Retell yesterday in the past tense",
    "intro": "To tell what you did, use the perfect tense and put _herī_ (yesterday) first. For “I” the ending is always _-ī_: _surrēxī_ (I got up), _lāvī_ (I washed), _ēdī_ (I ate), _vīdī_ (I saw), _iī_ (I went), _dormīvī_ (I slept). The stem changes from verb to verb, so each one is worth learning as a pair: _surgō / surrēxī_.",
    "ordered": true,
    "play": "narrate"
  },
